{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HoefsmitBBarParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.HoefsmitBBarParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uSq_bar_covariance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uSq_bar_covariance","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L79-L90","doc":"**The corrected ladder covariance**: `u²(q⁻¹) = q⁴·u²(q)`, i.e.\n`u ↦ +q²·u` under the bar involution — `u` is bar-EVEN-covariant.\n\nThis is the load-bearing correction: the criterion-2b prune asserted\n`u ↦ −q²·u` (bar-odd-covariant) from a non-canonical `b`; the canonical\n`b` (bar-even) gives `+q²` with **no sign**, so the bar-even-kernel law on\nthe coefficients is `c_k(q⁻¹) = q^{−2k}·c_k(q)` with no `(−1)^k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.uSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.uSq","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L75-L77","doc":"The squared Q_β expansion variable `u² = b²·(ℏ_q²)²`.  (Working with the\nsquare avoids `Real.sqrt`, keeping everything a field identity.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbarQ_bar_odd_covariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbarQ_bar_odd_covariant","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L68-L73","doc":"`ℏ_q` is **bar-odd-covariant**: `ℏ_q(q⁻¹) = −q·ℏ_q(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L65-L66","doc":"`ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hoefsmitBSq_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hoefsmitBSq_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L55-L63","doc":"**`b²` is bar-even**: `b²(q⁻¹) = b²(q)`. The Hoefsmit ladder base is\ninvariant under the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hoefsmitBSq_eq_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hoefsmitBSq_eq_h","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L44-L53","doc":"`b²` written through the Hecke parameter `h = q − q⁻¹`:\n`b² = (h² + 3)/(h² + 4)` (the form used by the mainstream `c_k` probes).\nThis makes bar-evenness manifest, since `h²` is bar-even. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hoefsmitBSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hoefsmitBSq","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HoefsmitBBarParity.lean#L40-L42","doc":"The square of the canonical Hoefsmit ladder base,\n`b² = (q⁴ + q² + 1)/(q² + 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}